/dev stands for Devices.
Contains special files representing hardware.
Allows user-space access to kernel drivers.
Includes block (storage) and character (serial) devices.

Virtual Consoles: tty1–tty6 are local text terminals.

Serial Ports: ttyS0–ttySN represent hardware serial interfaces.

Current Console: tty0 refers to the active virtual console.

ARM Serial: ttyAMA0 is specific to ARM-based systems.

Permissions: Typically owned by root:tty or root:dialout.

Access Control: Users must be in tty or dialout group.

Configuration: Serial settings managed via stty command.

Kernel Output: ttyprintk captures kernel printk messages.